-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Dynamite Dan
  Publisher   Mirrorsoft, 1985
  Version     1.1

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Dynamite Dan (1985)(Mirrorsoft).z80
  MD5         3470d12b21edb24d6b665dfac5e8d84d

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures become Next hardware sprites, so they keep their own colours
  and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is unchanged.

  Pace        original (+0.09% measured in JNext 1.1.104 headless, the default
              build (its keys code adds 3 T a tick); probe 0xC80A (the main
              loop, once a tick); input keyed to ticks; lockstep on lives and
              room; 10 trials per scene of up to 300 ticks (the mean; single
              trials -0.6 to +0.5 percent))

  Changes     1.0: Dan as Next sprites, the airship's hull and cables in front
              of him; Sinclair's 48K ROM as the whole alt ROM, so the game
              starts from its own BASIC; the game's speed restored after every
              hook; R kept as the original's
              1.1: QUIT and PAUSE can be redefined (option, on by default)

  Note        Keys: a key on the loading screen, then ENTER on the menu. In
              play A left, S right, SPACE jump, P pause, Q quit (the
              defaults). On by default, all five can be set on the game's own
              define-keys page (D on its menu), which now asks for QUIT and
              PAUSE after LEFT, RIGHT and JUMP, in its own style, and no
              longer warns about Q and P; the patch's menu line "Original keys
              (Q,P fixed)" gives v1.0's game exactly. As in the original, the
              page takes any key, a repeat included, and the game's menu and
              instructions show the default keys. The "Disable Q quit key"
              cheat disables whichever key is set for QUIT. Dan is a Next
              sprite in bright cyan over his own pixels, the look the owner
              approved, and in the airship room the hull and cables are drawn
              in front of him, so he stands inside the basket; the rooms,
              enemies and panel keep the original's colours. The hook costs
              about 0.1 percent of the game's pace (never faster); the game
              has no padding to repay it from. It starts from the tape's own
              BASIC. Cheats from the archive's POKEs for this release (two
              names shortened for the menu: Energy bar never decreases,
              Disable "Q Quit" key); dropped: Manipulate teleports, Water
              can't kill you, Picked up oxygen bottle and Speed up game (their
              code was never reached in the simulator's play, so not shown to
              work), Dynamite sticks found (asks for a value). Dan's sprite
              moves as his plot starts, so once in a few hundred frames it is
              a frame ahead of the game's own pixels under it. Not tested on
              hardware.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite lives
   2  No enemies
   3  Energy never decreases
   4  Disable Q quit key

  Cheats come from the archive's POKEs for this release.

