-- TESTING -------------------------------------------------------------------
  Tested      Played by the owner in JNext 2026-11-05, with QUIT and PAUSE
              redefined: approved

  Replay      v1.0's hooks: IDENTICAL on 52 recordings, 122,380 frames: 22,117
              Dan plots, 269 screen clears (the ending's hide in unit cases
              only): at every hook original and patched code compared from the
              same state, every register with R, memory, Dan's sprite pixels
              against the original plotter's ink, the airship's hull and
              cables against the live screen in room 43; 27 negative controls
              detected; ROM path check clean, the BASIC start included. v1.1's
              keys (246 bytes, disjoint from the hooks): the original against
              the original with them, in lockstep on the same 52 recordings,
              every IN served in order (192,925 reads), all 22,425 main-loop
              passes compared (every register but A and F, dead there; R
              included; all RAM outside the patch): IDENTICAL with Q and P,
              and with QUIT X and PAUSE H set by the build's own define
              routine; 3 broken builds detected (play reading the old P, the
              old Q; R 4 off); 6,290 unit cases 0 failures (pause, quit, the
              old P and Q held, every key as PAUSE or QUIT, the Q cheat on and
              off)

  Emulator    JNext 1.1.104 headless, the default build from its own BASIC:
              the define page without the Q / P warning, five prompts, X and H
              stored; in play the old P and Q held 30 ticks each do nothing, H
              pauses and H resumes, X quits to the menu; the same through the
              .nxc's menu build; the menu build against the bare build
              (defaults, the toggle, all cheats, both): every listed bank and
              register but R the same; flicker check over 300 frames: as v1.0
              (1 frame with Dan's sprite a frame ahead of his own ULA pixels,
              1 one-frame attribute change also in the approved build);
              15-minute soak: no freeze, loop or crash

  Coverage    Random-play recordings only, no human play: one from the TOSEC
              file's BASIC start (rooms 0, 43, 44), 48 room-census starts,
              deaths, water, the airship room; none pauses or quits (those by
              unit cases and JNext); not reached: the ending (all 8 dynamite
              sticks and the airship), the lifts measured

  Hardware    none

  Nothing here claims a result on real hardware unless the line above says so.

-- HOW TO USE ----------------------------------------------------------------
  Put this .nxc and the game file in the same folder on the Next's card and
  choose the .nxc in the Browser. See README.txt.
